-// CityRotation.cs - daily LiveOps city-front rotation for MobTide (G07-T015).
-// The siege stands at a different city every day: one of seven embedded
-// garrison themes (the config ships in the build - zero server, red line 12)
-// rotates on the very day key the ad cap already flips on (one boundary),
-// and the featured front city rides the same integer seed (dayseed % 30 -
-// the SaveWire city-mask cap), so every device reads the same front on the
-// same local day: same day, all ends, one city. The clock is device-local
-// degradation: TodayKey() is the single time face and a malformed key
-// degrades to seed 0 deterministically - never throws, never calls out.
-// Derivation is pure integer math: two derives of one key are byte-identical
-// through both the string face and the seed face. The rotation owns only its
-// own faces - the front banner line and its accent (TideStageView); the tide
-// engine, the wave table and the resolver constants stay byte-identical
-// whatever the day brings (RotationCheck proves the event stream never moves).
-// Festival window (G07-T032 LiveOps holiday skin): local calendar days
-// 10-01..10-08 flip the banner line and its accent to the HOLIDAY TIDE skin -
-// window-scoped override only, the theme/city derives and every engine face
-// stay byte-identical, outside the window the classic front resets exactly,
-// and the window recurs every year (same day, all ends, one skin).
