-// StayFlow.cs - S1 night-stay offline settlement core (T006): ports the frozen E4
-// graybox M8 face into the real runtime. Morning settlement of overnight stayers:
-// away earnings = stayers x rate x the frozen 8.0h away window, capped per night
-// (base(2)=16, five stayers cap at 20). The X973 dual-anchor wall-clock domain guards
-// the offline face: the save ledger carries WallSavedAt + UptimeSavedAt, a resume with
-// a rolled-back wall clock clamps the away window to zero (zero pay, zero double
-// pay), and a fresh ledger without anchors never grants free coins. A settled night
-// never pays twice: the last-settled-night key makes every settlement idempotent no
-// matter which clock face calls it, and the offline gate reuses the same settle core
-// so there is exactly one settlement path (zero future drift). The wallet is
-// injected per call (ServeShift.Wallet stays the single economy source). Pure C#
-// (no UnityEngine) so Editor gates drive it headless; the view layer binds in T009.
-// Every number is a frozen E4 anchor (GrayboxSim.cs) - zero re-tuning, zero RNG.
