-// GrayboxSim.cs
-// GrayboxSim.cs - pure C# deterministic logic prototype for ArrowOut (E4 graybox, M6-B lane).
-// Arrow-escape board puzzle: tap an arrow, it slides on its own until it slams into a
-// wall, the border, or a stopped buddy arrow (a "pile"). Arrows leave the board
-// through edge gaps. Plan the ignition order so every arrow escapes. The self-slide
-// is the 3-second perceivable identity vs draw/drag neighbors (E1 face): one tap,
-// then the arrow crosses the whole lane with zero further input. A stopped arrow is
-// a pile that blocks lanes and unblocks its dependents when it escapes (chain depth
-// face). Ghost / turner / double arrows are the mechanism vocabulary (U023 axes).
-// The "one cell short" mutual block is the near-miss beat with optional IAA outs
-// (pile rescue / level skip / move hint) - purely optional, the campaign closes with
-// zero ads. Banned vocab (E1 guardrails): the original Miniclip title and the G06
-// sibling name never appear on any face. Share face: board-clear achievement card
-// with an X032-style code, never a score form (B904 guardrail #2 analog).
-// No UnityEngine dependency: sim time is logical seconds; wall-clock perf is
-// measured by the editor check. Zero RNG by construction.
