-// ShareCodecCore.cs - S1 T009 share-codec core for ArrowOut (B1831 kit-port).
-// Ported under the kit-port law (G26 B1276 ShareCodecCore paradigm): every
-// frozen value stays verbatim - zero new tuning.
-// Frozen anchors (all traceable to the E4 kit, GrayboxSim.cs ShareCard face):
-//   - code prefix "AO1-" = kit ShareCard prefix verbatim (the share-code family mark)
-//   - compose face = kit ShareCard verbatim: the board-clear achievement card
-//     code = one uppercase hex digit of LevelsCompleted + "-" + the board arrow
-//     count - never a score form (B904 guardrail #2 analog; requirement M08
-//     "AO1- prefix share code, X032 offline shape (zero server), compose/decode
-//     round-trip", S05 ShareCodec ComposeCard/DecodeCard)
-//   - share-form ban = kit ShareFormTokens verbatim: score / points / rank
-//     never appear in any share payload face
-//   - campaign face = E4 assertion 6 verbatim: the five-board campaign fires
-//     exactly 4 cards (4 clears + 1 honest fail - a failed board shows off nothing)
-// Structural S1 extension vs the kit: the decode face (M08 requires a true
-// compose/decode round-trip; the kit only composed). The X032 offline shape is
-// structural: the code alone restores the run face with zero server and zero
-// external state (a fresh codec instance decodes any card identically).
-// Decode is strict: null / wrong prefix / empty payload / missing separator /
-// empty levels segment / non-hex levels char / empty count segment / non-digit
-// count char / zero-arrow count all reject with exactly one event each.
-// Zero state mutation: the codec observes the run; it never mutates anything.
-// Pure C#: zero UnityEngine.
